                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e8b3b9f7-04f7-3ae3-b54d-937203fdd6cf",
                        "entry_id": "3b4a86e9-547e-340d-b282-b3d59bc9dd9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сухие или гнилые сучья, деревья, лежащие на земле"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "847e2f64-0d0b-406a-ae1d-e83293ff6251",
                                "sense_id": "e8b3b9f7-04f7-3ae3-b54d-937203fdd6cf",
                                "text": "Кедровые сучья, перемешанные с валежником, с покалеченным, искорёженным молодняком, повсюду высились в завалах — не перелезть…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4b42e03-5fde-4321-8920-20f6634a27a7",
                                "sense_id": "e8b3b9f7-04f7-3ae3-b54d-937203fdd6cf",
                                "text": "Вскоре валежник затрещал под ногами проводника, и он вышел на тропу с веткой лавровишни, густо усеянной гроздьями ягод."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df72758d-8c50-4978-9e43-6493f3afecf7",
                                "sense_id": "e8b3b9f7-04f7-3ae3-b54d-937203fdd6cf",
                                "text": "А Егор упоённо чистил лес, прорубал заросшие просеки, стаскивал в кучи валежник и сухостой."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e43ebdb-3293-4e59-8556-538c492e588c",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b4a86e9-547e-340d-b282-b3d59bc9dd9a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e8b3b9f7-04f7-3ae3-b54d-937203fdd6cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "brushwood",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brushwood",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10e7db9d-2640-3446-8416-30d0e895c266",
                                        "entry_id": "6d62511b-24aa-3e14-9844-28f15dfff97b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Branches and twigs fallen from trees and shrubs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43ce4e02-13b7-4305-9a2e-c21b826ade07",
                                                "sense_id": "10e7db9d-2640-3446-8416-30d0e895c266",
                                                "text": "His pupils assemble every evening before his tent; where, by the light of a large fire, made of brushwood and cow’s dung, they are taught a few sentences from the Koran, and are initiated into the principles of their creed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b103f29-14d4-4f97-aa54-933eaeac2c17",
                                                "sense_id": "10e7db9d-2640-3446-8416-30d0e895c266",
                                                "text": "Small streams with hollowed-out banks came into sight, and the tiniest mill-ponds with frail dams, and little villages with low peasant huts under dark roofs, often with half their thatch gone, and small threshing barns all tilted to one side with walls made out of woven brushwood and gaping openings beside dilabidated hay-barns […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "252da3e2-80dd-37fc-8d84-82d487357769",
                                        "entry_id": "6d62511b-24aa-3e14-9844-28f15dfff97b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small trees and shrubs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9a55cd9-8a0b-413d-bf19-e2254c991301",
                                                "sense_id": "252da3e2-80dd-37fc-8d84-82d487357769",
                                                "text": "The river above Goet-accord becomes very narrow, being lined on each ſide with impenetrable bruſh-wood, like the river Cottica, between Devil's-Harwar and Patamaca; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2780ab3b-ce35-4926-a570-cbd435b278af",
                                                "sense_id": "252da3e2-80dd-37fc-8d84-82d487357769",
                                                "text": "Without any solicitation, or desire for profit on his part, he had been asked to execute during that winter a very large order for hurdles and other copseware, for which purpose he had been obliged to buy several acres of brushwood standing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f76d691e-7c62-412f-b174-9e4096364b2e",
                                                "sense_id": "252da3e2-80dd-37fc-8d84-82d487357769",
                                                "text": "Houses had been deserted, and the thick brushwood of the tropics had grown up over everything, obliterating the brief authority of man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ce68f2d-03b5-4697-b906-f112309b1908",
                                                "sense_id": "252da3e2-80dd-37fc-8d84-82d487357769",
                                                "text": "Mr. Greenshields was the contractor selected to build the embankment, and over a hundred thousand tons of marl and moss compacted with brushwood were used in its construction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
